    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `5c1edd03f`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`df9ec30b6`, merged in). The author's checks are green on this head: `cargo check --tests` for pathkernel and motion, the `laws` suite (140 passed), the motion `kernel_laws` suite (30 passed), clippy, the quick gate against the side branch (4 steps) and the light lane (7 steps). The writer record on #4254 is released. The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and has `Refs #4254`. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer. The safety floor applies: this rule lets the tool stay down on the way from the air into the stock.\n- The claim of the PR: 0 lifts and 0 crossing feeds for the material side Outside on the disc band and the dog-bone band (13 and 15 before). The earlier zero of PR #4234 came from an assumption that a review refused. Check that this zero is a proof: the approach stretch cuts no stock that the next piece does not cut (the exact area check in `link/approach.rs`), and the negative pin with a tooth of stock beside the start fails when that check is off.\n- The PR changes two existing pins: one test in `link_rule.rs` that pinned the old refusal of the way back in from the air, and the Outside rows of `k3_load.rs` (the approach stretches read as over-limit moves with no name). Check that each change is the measured new fact and not a weaker pin.\n- One approach on the dog bone meets fresh stock at full width. No stage reads that yet. The author filed #4272.\n- The trial merge and the gate base are `origin/side/path-kernel`.",
